e solutions to the same system of linear ODEs, then ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nIn our case, our Wronskian is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({x}_{1},{x}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\cdot {e}^{2t}-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & ={e}^{4t} \\\\  & ={e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is $\\text{nonzero for at least one }t\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the set ${{x}_{1}(t),{x}_{2}(t)}$ is linearly $\\text{independent}$ on $R.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee461d3e-3afa-51c6-bddd-355668cac3ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent Vector-Valued Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5c5fda0-a874-5669-be50-630aaf890a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220562} {:answer/id #uuid "46f59fe6-486f-5c5e-8989-4d1fb36fe25f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220563} {:answer/id #uuid "733af770-dc3c-5023-81a3-4cfb4245f5cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "− 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220564} {:answer/id #uuid "79c3be04-cfbf-52e9-9730-c962ff4a98aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos (2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5c5fda0-a874-5669-be50-630aaf890a76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220562} :answer-field/id #uuid "698fd7a3-feb4-5cca-8334-9ab6921a31ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220561} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274328b2-11b2-577d-8d62-37e787cb69f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "dependent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220567} {:answer/id #uuid "65d1ddc8-d69b-50e2-bd3c-aa1a9c0ed8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text